    "labelChirho": "embroiderer, variegator (Qal participle)",
    "descriptionChirho": "Active Qal participial form of raqam meaning 'one who embroiders' or 'variegator,' referring to a skilled artisan who works multicolored designs into fabric. Attested 8x as a designation of craftsmanship in tabernacle/temple contexts. Evidence: eng 'embroiderer,' spa 'bordador,' arb 'مُطَرِّزٍ' (one who embroiders), kor '수놓은 자의' (one who embroidered), swa 'ya mtarizi' (of the embroiderer), hin 'कढ़ाई की' (of embroidery). All translations consistently render an active agent noun for textile artisanship.",
