    "labelChirho": "was intricately woven (Pual passive)",
    "descriptionChirho": "Pual (intensive passive) participial form of raqam meaning 'to be intricately woven together,' used metaphorically in Psalm 139:15 of being formed in the womb. The passive stem marks a genuinely distinct sense from the active Qal participle. Evidence: eng 'I was woven,' spa 'fui entretejido' (I was interwoven), arb 'نُسِجْتُ' (I was woven), kor '엮어졌나이다' (was interlaced), swa 'niliposukwa' (I was woven), hin 'बुना गया मैं' (I was woven). All translations use passive voice and metaphorical register.",
